WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.825
By day, fishing vessels use shapes.

2
00:00:03.075 --> 00:00:08.975
A vessel engaged in fishing shows two cones with their points together, one above the other.

3
00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:11.275
It looks like an hourglass.

4
00:00:11.525 --> 00:00:19.250
And when her gear extends more than one hundred fifty meters, she adds a single cone, point up, in the direction of the gear.

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.925
Same idea as the white light at night: it points to where the gear is.

6
00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:29.000
Now the other half of the rule, and it’s a favorite on the exam.

7
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:36.650
When a fishing vessel isn’t engaged in fishing, she shows only the ordinary lights or shapes for a vessel of her length.

8
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.300
So think of a shrimper steaming home before dawn with her nets stowed.

9
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.175
What does she show?

10
00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:45.550
Plain power-driven lights.

11
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.625
And what privileges does she have over you?

12
00:00:48.875 --> 00:00:50.200
None.

13
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.325
She’s just another power-driven vessel.
